<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδᾰπός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from what country?</i>: hence, generally, <i>whence?
				where born?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.218
			</span></i> (as v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				575
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1160
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				276
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς καὶ π.;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					20b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸ γένος;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					186
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				108
			</span></i>; of wine, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὁ Βρόμιος; Θάσιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					230
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>of what sort?</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸ δῶρον;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					453
				</span></i>
			: freq. in later Gr., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				8.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				1.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Inv.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>, etc.; in a play on both senses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸ γένος; πλούσιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					90
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύων</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; οἷος . . μὴ δάκνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					25.40
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
				</span></i>
			 Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.925
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταπῶς</span>
			<u>Gloss.</u> (<i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				39
			</span></i> considers signf. <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i> un-Attic, but S.l.c. is cited by Sch. D.T.<i><span class="en">
				p.239
			</span></i> H.: the spelling <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταπός</span></b>  (wh. is f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				230
			</span></i> (codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>)) is found in later Gr., ll. cc. supr., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.25J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.157
			</span></i>(v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				3.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Par.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				4.138c
			</span></i>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδ-</span>
			= Lat. <i>quod;</i> for the termination cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλοδαπός</span> (and v.
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				20.15
			</span></i>). Derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποίου
			δαπέδου</span> by Phryn.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>)</div>
